- hut: wood 10 → repair cost ceil(10/2)=5 wood
- farm: wood 15, stone 5 → repair cost ceil(15/2)=8 wood, ceil(5/2)=3 stone (round
ing-up case: farm's wood is odd at 15 → 8; stone 5 → 3)
- quarry: wood 20 → repair cost 10 wood

Building behaviors:
1. Repairs an already-built building at half the original cost (rounded up per resource
)
2. If the settlement doesn't have that building, does nothing (no-op) — returns the
 same settlement (in fact, returns the same object reference)
3. Never takes resources below 0 — clamps at 0

